   100	The charge states, as pinned background:
   101	
   102	> `F` is étale, so `E` has exactly `a` singular points, each ANALYTICALLY
   103	> a `(p,q)` cusp.
   104	
   105	The count `a` is right for a **generic** point of `A_F` and wrong for the
   106	**cusp** point. The two are separated by exactly one fact: at a generic
   107	`y in A_F` the local group is cyclic, at the cusp `c` it is the whole
   108	global group.
   109	
   110	> **THEOREM NO-CUSP-PREIMAGE.** Let `F : C^2 -> C^2` be Keller of degree
   111	> `N >= 2` with non-properness set `A_F`, let `c in A_F` be a point such
   112	> that `pi_1(B_c \ A_F) -> pi_1(C^2 \ A_F)` is **surjective** for a small
   113	> ball `B_c`. Then `F^{-1}(c) = empty`.
   114	>
   115	> *Proof.* `F` is proper over `X := C^2 \ A_F` and étale, so
   116	> `F : Y := C^2 \ E -> X` is a covering of degree `N`, `E := F^{-1}(A_F)`;
   117	> `Y` is connected (complement of a curve in `C^2`), so the classifying
   118	> `rho : pi_1(X) -> S_N` is transitive. Suppose `x in F^{-1}(c)`. Étale
   119	> means local biholomorphism: choose `U ni x` with `F|_U : U -> F(U)`
   120	> biholomorphic, then shrink `B := B_c` inside `F(U)` (`F` is étale hence
   121	> quasi-finite, so `F^{-1}(c)` is finite and one `B` serves all of it). Put
   122	> `U' := (F|_U)^{-1}(B)`. Then `F : U' \ E -> B \ A_F` is a homeomorphism,
   123	> i.e. a **section** of the covering `Y -> X` restricted over `B \ A_F`.
   124	> The image of a section over a connected base is a connected component of
   125	> the restricted covering. But the restriction of `Y -> X` over `B \ A_F`
   126	> is classified by `rho` composed with the surjection
   127	> `pi_1(B \ A_F) ->> pi_1(X)`, hence has the same orbits as `rho`, hence
   128	> is connected of degree `N`. So `N = 1`. Contradiction. ∎
   129	
   130	> **COROLLARY.** In case (A), `A_F = {x^p = y^q}` (Lin–Zaidenberg via
   131	> MPRIME Prop. 7.1) is a cone: with the weighted `C^*`-action
   132	> `lambda.(x,y) = (lambda^q x, lambda^p y)` both `C^2 \ A_F` and
   133	> `B_eps \ A_F` deformation-retract onto the same weighted-sphere
   134	> complement `S^3 \ T(p,q)`, compatibly with inclusion, so
   135	> `pi_1(B_c \ A_F) -> pi_1(C^2 \ A_F)` is an **isomorphism**. Hence
   136	> `F^{-1}(c) = empty`, `E` is a **smooth** affine curve (its only possible
   137	> singularities were the analytic cusps over `c`), its `j` components are
   138	> pairwise **disjoint**, and
   139	> `F|_E : E -> A_F \ {c} = C^*` is étale.
   140	
   141	The corresponding true statement about `a` is the one HT already has:
   142	`a = #Fix(rho(m))` is the number of preimages of a **generic** point of
   143	`A_F` (HT (3.1), HV §5, both confirmed). Nothing in HT, HV or SW is
   144	retracted by this: none of CENTRAL-RANK, ORBIFOLD-CAGE, CUSP-PARITY,
   145	CUSP-A-EMPTY uses a preimage of `c`. **Flagged, not claimed:** MPRIME
   146	Prop. 6.1 is quoted by SW §7 as "unique unibranch cusp, `K_p = a-1`,
   147	`a_p = 1`"; MPRIME is not charged to me and I cannot check whether its
   148	`K_p` ledger is a statement about `E` (in which case the premise
   149	`F^{-1}(c) != empty` there needs re-reading) or about the dicritical map
   150	to `A_F` (in which case it is untouched). That is a cross-check request
   151	for the coordinator, not a correction.
