   153	## 3. Chain I — the Euler gate closes case (A) at every degree
   154	
   155	This is the charge's item (G-C), run to the end. Every number in it is
   156	either pinned by the record or eliminated.
   157	
   158	> **THEOREM CUSP-A-VOID.** There is no Keller map `F : C^2 -> C^2` of
   159	> degree `N >= 2` whose non-properness set `A_F` is homeomorphic to `C`
   160	> and singular. Equivalently: MPRIME case (A) is EMPTY at every degree.
   161	>
   162	> *Proof.* By Lin–Zaidenberg, `A_F ~ {x^p = y^q}` under `Aut(C^2)`, with
   163	> `p, q >= 2` coprime; assume this normalisation.
   164	>
   165	> **(i) Euler.** `chi(A_F) = chi(C) = 1`, so `chi(X) = chi(C^2) - chi(A_F)
   166	> = 1 - 1 = 0`. `Y -> X` is an `N`-fold covering, so `chi(Y) = N chi(X)
   167	> = 0`. Additivity of `chi = chi_c` for complex algebraic varieties gives
   168	> ```text
   169	>     chi(E) = chi(C^2) - chi(Y) = 1 - 0 = 1 .
   170	> ```
   171	> **(ii) Structure of `E`.** By THEOREM NO-CUSP-PREIMAGE, `E` is smooth,
   172	> so its `j` irreducible components `E_1,...,E_j` are pairwise disjoint
   173	> and `chi(E) = sum_i chi(E_i)`. Each `E_i` is a smooth irreducible affine
   174	> curve: `E_i = bar E_i \ S_i` with `bar E_i` smooth projective of genus
   175	> `g_i` and `theta_i := |S_i| >= 1` places at infinity, so
   176	> ```text
   177	>     chi(E_i) = 2 - 2 g_i - theta_i  <=  1 ,
   178	>     with equality iff  g_i = 0 and theta_i = 1, i.e. iff  E_i =~ A^1 .
   179	> ```
   180	> **(iii) The forced `A^1`.** The `chi(E_i)` are integers `<= 1` summing to
   181	> `1`, so at least one of them equals `1`: some component is `=~ A^1`.
   182	>
   183	> **(iv) The contradiction.** `F` is étale, so `dF` is invertible and no
   184	> component of `E` is contracted; hence `F|_{E_i} : E_i -> A_F` is
   185	> non-constant. By NO-CUSP-PREIMAGE its image avoids `c`, and
   186	> `A_F \ {c} =~ C^*` (the normalisation `t |-> (t^q, t^p)` is an
   187	> isomorphism off the singular point). So `F|_{E_i}` is a non-constant
   188	> morphism `A^1 -> C^*`, i.e. a non-constant unit of `C[t]`. There is
   189	> none. ∎
   190	
   191	**The same computation, in the form the charge asks for.** Writing
   192	`nu := #F^{-1}(c)` (the number of cusps of `E`, `= 0` by §2) and
   193	`Sigma^* := sum_i sum_{P in S_i^*} e_P >= 0`, where `S_i^*` is the set of
   194	places of `E_i` at infinity lying over `C^* = A_F \ {c}` and `e_P` the
   195	ramification index of `bar E_i -> P^1` there, Riemann–Hurwitz for
   196	`bar E_i -> P^1` (unramified at every point of `E_i`, because `F` is a
   197	local isomorphism and the normalisation of a `(p,q)` cusp maps
   198	isomorphically to the normalisation of `A_F`) gives the **exact identity**
   199	
   200	```text
   201	   (G-C)      chi(E)  =  nu  -  Sigma^*        and     chi(E) = 1 .
   202	```
   203	
   204	So the charged identity is `nu = 1 + Sigma^* >= 1`: a Keller counterexample
   205	in case (A) would need at least one cusp on `E`. §2 says `nu = 0`. That
   206	is the mismatch, and a mismatch is a kill.
   207	
   208	**What the record pins, and what it does not.** Pinned by the charged
   209	record: `N`, `j = rank H^ab`, `a = #Fix(rho(m))`, `kappa`, `M`, `W = N-a`,
   210	the dicritical partition `(s_l, mu_l)` of `W`, the meridian cycle type.
   211	Derived here and *not* previously pinned: `chi(E) = 1`; `nu = 0`; `E`
   212	smooth; components disjoint; `chi(E_i) = -sum_{S_i^*} e_P <= 0` for every
   213	`i`. Still **not** pinned by anything (and not needed): the individual
   214	`g_i`, `theta_i`, the component degrees `d_i` over `A_F`, the ramification
   215	profile at infinity, and hence the link at infinity `K_infty` of `E` and
   216	its `Delta_infty`. The Euler gate closes without any of them, which is
   217	exactly why it beats (G-A) (§6).
   218	
   219	**Scope.** Chain I uses only: `A_F` homeomorphic to `C` and singular; `F`
   220	étale; `N >= 2`. It does **not** use `H2`, CUSP-KILL, 7.B, CUSP-PARITY,
   221	ORBIFOLD-CAGE, CENTRAL-RANK, or any homology of the cover. It is not a
   222	strengthening of the cage; it is a different argument. Under `H2`, case
   223	(A) is exactly the branch it kills. Composed with the banked SMOOTH-KILL
   224	**at SMOOTH-KILL's own typing** (not re-derived here, its hypotheses not
   225	checked here) it would read: *the non-properness set of a noninvertible
   226	Keller map is never homeomorphic to `C`* — recorded as a consequence,
   227	not asserted.
