   526	   `rho(m)`-fixed sheets in one `<rho(z)>`-block, so the two meridian
   527	   lifts are conjugate in `H` and carry the *same* class in
   528	   `H^ab = Z^2`. A two-component plane curve complement has two
   529	   *independent* meridians (Lemma F1). MEASURED: `ndist = 1`. Kill.
