   161	one gets a genuine, usable consequence in the *opposite* direction:
   162	`H^ab = Z^{r(E)}` is a **quotient** of `Lambda^{ab}`, so
   163	
   164	```text
   165	(Q1)  r(E)  <=  rank Lambda^{ab} ,   and
   166	(Q2)  the global relators must kill the whole torsion of Lambda^{ab}.
   167	```
   168	
   169	At DISC's `(9,6,2)` cabled place, `Lambda^{ab} = Z^3 (+) Z/2` on all 144
   170	tuples, so `(Q1)` reads `r(E) <= 3` and `(Q2)` says the affine tangency
   171	and node relators must annihilate the measured `Z/2`. Both are typed
   172	**conditional on `(M-surj)`**, which is *not* banked:
   173	
   174	```text
   175	OPEN[HOMCOVER-LINK-INFTY-SURJ]   Is  pi_1(S^3_R \ K_infty) -> pi_1(C^2 \ A)
   176	                                 surjective for R >> 0 ?
   177	```
   178	
   179	Status of that OPEN, honestly. The Morse/handle argument ("build
   180	`B_R \ A` from the collar with handles of index `>= 2`") does not run as
   181	written: `|z|^2` is not proper on the Stein surface `C^2 \ A`, and the
   182	statement is false for general properly embedded surfaces in `B^4`, so
   183	complex-analyticity must be used and I found no clean primary source for
   184	the affine-curve case. Hamm-type Lefschetz theory at infinity gives
   185	`pi_1(∂W) ↠ pi_1(W)` for the **full** boundary of a compact model, which
   186	includes the tube around `A` and is weaker (it amounts to "generated by
   187	meridians"). Checked by hand on the cuspidal cubic, `{xy=1}` and
   188	`{y=x^2}`: iso, `Z^2 ↠ Z`, iso. Not promoted; not used below.
   189	
   190	### 2.3 (F3) Characteristic-variety custody — and why it does not apply
   191	
   192	The charge's item (1)(a) asks whether Libgober-type theory is available
   193	for **affine** complements. Custody answer, by name:
   194	
   195	* **Arapura**, *Geometry of cohomology support loci for local systems I*,
   196	  J. Algebraic Geom. 6 (1997) 563–597 — structure of `V_1(X)` for `X`
   197	  smooth **quasi-projective**; `C^2 \ A` is quasi-projective, so this is
   198	  the correct primary source, and it is stronger than the projective-only
   199	  reading. Positive-dimensional components are pullbacks along maps to
   200	  curves; translation by torsion characters (Simpson; Budur–Wang).
   201	* **Libgober**, *Alexander polynomial of plane algebraic curves and
   202	  cyclic multiple planes*, Duke Math. J. 49 (1982) 833–851, and
   203	  *Characteristic varieties of algebraic curves* (2001) — divisibility of
   204	  the Alexander polynomial by local polynomials and by the polynomial at
   205	  infinity. This is the only genuine **local-to-global** theorem in the
   206	  area.
   207	
   208	Both are characteristic-**zero** statements about **abelian** covers.
   209	That is fatal here, and the campaign's own ledger says why:
   210	
   211	> **COR 7.2 (MPRIME §7, PROVED-HERE, consumed).** For a noninvertible
   212	> plane Keller map, `rho` is transitive but **not regular**.
   213	
   214	A transitive **abelian** subgroup of `S_N` is regular. Hence
   215	`rho(G)` is nonabelian at every degree, `rho` never factors through
   216	`H_1(C^2\A)`, and the ACS-1 covering is **never** an abelian cover.
   217	Libgober's divisibility and Arapura's structure theorem compute the
   218	homology of abelian covers; they do not compute `H_1` of an irregular
   219	cover. Using them here would be a place/series identification.
   220	
   221	The correct reformulation, which *is* the right object, is modular:
   222	
   223	> **LEMMA MOD-P.** With `Gamma := rho(G)`, `Gamma_1` the point stabiliser,
   224	> and `t_p` the number of cyclic `p`-power summands of `H^ab`,
   225	> ```text
   226	> t_p  =  dim_{F_p} H_1(X ; F_p[Gamma/Gamma_1])  -  dim_Q H_1(X ; Q[Gamma/Gamma_1]).
   227	> ```
   228	> *Proof.* Shapiro plus universal coefficients (`H_0(X~;Z) = Z` is
   229	> torsion-free, so the `H_0` correction term vanishes). ∎
   230	
   231	So "`H^ab` has torsion" is exactly "the induced permutation local system
   232	**jumps in characteristic `p`**". At `p = 2`, `N = 4`, the permutation
   233	module `F_2[S_4/S_3]` is non-semisimple with composition factors
   234	`triv, 2-dim, triv` — two trivial factors instead of one — which is the
   235	structural reason `Z/2` is the torsion DISC keeps measuring. The
   236	literature for such jumps is **Papadima–Suciu** modular resonance
   237	(e.g. Proc. LMS 114 (2017) 961–1004) and **Cohen–Denham–Suciu** torsion
   238	in Milnor fibres. To my knowledge there is **no** local-to-global
   239	divisibility theorem for mod-`p` Betti numbers of irregular covers of
   240	curve complements. Typed:
   241	
   242	```text
   243	OPEN[HOMCOVER-MODP-DIVISIBILITY]  a Libgober-type local-to-global bound for
   244	                                  dim H^1(X; F_p[Gamma/Gamma_1]).  Not in the
   245	                                  literature I can name; not derived here.
   246	```
   247	
   248	That OPEN, not the discriminator's measurement, is the real obstacle to
   249	the charged theorem — and THEOREM NO-PUSHFORWARD says even a positive
   250	answer would not by itself deliver it.
   251	
   252	## 3. The constraint interface at general `N`
   253	
   254	### 3.1 The meridian cycle type, and `a = #Fix` exactly
   255	
   256	MPRIME Lemma 4.1 / `[P3]` give `N = a + sum_l s_l mu_l` and the generic
   257	meridian cycle type `1^a · prod_l mu_l^{s_l}`; THEOREM 7.B' gives
   258	`mu_l >= 2` for every dicritical under `H2`. Hence every nontrivial cycle
   259	of `rho(m)` has length `>= 2` and
   260	
   261	```text
   262	(3.1)   #Fix(rho(m_i))  =  a^{(i)}  =  N - W_i      exactly.
   263	```
   264	
   265	This closes `OPEN[ACS-FIX-VS-DEFICIT]` (ID §4) in the affirmative **at
   266	the scope `H2` + 7.B**: the inequality ID insisted on is an equality
   267	there, because the only way to lose the equality is a `mu_l = 1`
   268	dicritical and 7.B forbids one. ID's caution was correct and its
   269	counterexample (`W_2 = 1`, `a^{(2)} = 3`, no element of `S_4` with three
   270	fixed points) lives in the **reducible** profile, where `H2` fails and
   271	`D_2` is a second component — outside this scope. Both statements stand;
   272	they are about different profiles. I use only (3.1), and only under `H2`.
   273	
   274	### 3.2 Non-regularity
   275	
   276	COR 7.2, quoted verbatim above, is profile-free and I use it twice: to
   277	kill abelian theory (§2.3) and as a discard rule in the `N = 8` census
   278	(§5.5). It is MPRIME's, PROVED-HERE/UNREVIEWED there; I consume it at
   279	that typing and do not upgrade it.
   280	
   281	### 3.3 "Cabled place" at general `N` — `OPEN[CABLE-UNIVERSALITY]`
   282	
   283	The charge asks for the exact banked form of "a counterexample's `A`
   284	components are never transverse to `L_infty`", citing ROWKILL. **It is
   285	not there.** ROWKILL is the `S_4` row-kill integration; it contains no
   286	transversality-at-infinity statement, and a full-tree search finds the
   287	phrase only in ID §5 itself, where it is asserted without citation. The
   288	nearest banked all-`N` statement is MPRIME:
   289	
   290	> **LEMMA A** (MPRIME §2): under `H2` the normalization of `A_F` is `A^1`.
   291	> Hence `A_F` is rational with **exactly one place at infinity**
   292	> (`theta = 1`, MPRIME §1.2 and §9).
   293	
   294	One place at infinity on a curve whose projective closure has degree
   295	`n >= 3` (SMOOTH-KILL forces `A_F` singular, and a singular irreducible
   296	plane curve has degree `>= 3`) means the single place has contact `n` with
   297	`L_infty` — certainly not `n` transverse points. So the *transversality*
   298	half of ID's assertion is banked under `H2`. What is **not** banked is
   299	that the place is *cabled* in the sense that matters (nontrivial Puiseux
   300	characteristic, i.e. `K_infty` not the unknot): a smooth branch with
   301	contact `n` gives an unknotted link at infinity, as `{y = x^n}` shows.
   302	Typed:
   303	
   304	```text
   305	OPEN[CABLE-UNIVERSALITY]  Under H2, is the unique place of A_F at infinity
   306	                          always of nontrivial Puiseux type?  Banked: one
   307	                          place, non-transverse.  Not banked: nontrivial cable.
   308	```
   309	
   310	For the substrate this lane actually uses this OPEN is **discharged**, and
   311	that is one reason to use it: in case (A), `A_F ≅_{Aut} {x^p=y^q}` with
   312	`p,q >= 2`, and the complement is `S^3 \ T(p,q)` with `T(p,q)` a genuine
   313	nontrivial torus knot (Lin–Zaidenberg + the cone structure). Cabled, at
   314	every degree, with proof.
   315	
   316	### 3.4 `TB-GERM` / `CABLE-3` at general `N`
   317	
   318	DISC's finding is confirmed and extended: `TB-GERM` (`beta_1 = 8 + 3kappa`)
   319	is a family-3 `(8,6)` statement, arithmetically inapplicable at `(9,6,2)`
