   355	
   356	## 5. The theorems on the merged substrate
   357	
   358	Fix case (A): `A_F ≅_{Aut(C^2)} {x^p=y^q}`, `p,q >= 2`, `gcd(p,q)=1`
   359	(MPRIME Prop. 7.1). Write `G = G_{p,q} = <alpha,beta | alpha^p = beta^q>`,
   360	`Z = Z(G) = <z>`, `z = alpha^p`; `H = rho^{-1}(Stab_1)` of index `N`;
   361	`E = F^{-1}(A_F)` with `j` components, `H^{ab} = Z^j` (Lemma F1);
   362	`Z_H = H ∩ Z`, `kappa = [Z:Z_H]`, `Delta = H/Z_H ≅ HZ/Z <= G/Z ≅ Z/p * Z/q`
   363	of index `M`, `N = M kappa`. The meridian is `m = alpha^e beta^f` with
   364	`eq + fp = 1` (so `m` generates `G^{ab} = Z`, where `alpha |-> q`,
   365	`beta |-> p`).
   366	
   367	### 5.1 THEOREM CENTRAL-RANK (`r = j - 1`)
   368	
   369	> **THEOREM CENTRAL-RANK.** Write `Delta ≅ F_r * C_1 * ... * C_k` (Kurosh;
   370	> `C_i` finite cyclic). Then `rank H^{ab} = r + 1`. Equivalently, for the
   371	> Keller reading, `r = j - 1`.
   372	>
   373	> *Proof.* `1 -> Z_H -> H -> Delta -> 1` is central (`Z_H <= Z(G)`), and
   374	> `Z_H ≅ Z` since `[Z : Z ∩ H] <= N`. `H_2(Delta) = 0`, because homology of
   375	> a free product is the direct sum of the homologies of the factors and
   376	> `H_2(F_r) = H_2(Z/n) = 0`. The five-term exact sequence
   377	> `H_2(Delta) -> Z_H -> H^{ab} -> Delta^{ab} -> 0` then makes
   378	> `Z_H ↪ H^{ab}` an infinite-order injection, so `rank H^{ab} =
   379	> rank Delta^{ab} + 1 = r + 1`. ∎
   380	
   381	MPRIME CUSP-CAGE states `r ∈ {j-1, j}`. The `r = j` alternative would
   382	require the image of `Z_H` in `H^{ab}` to be finite, which the five-term
   383	sequence forbids. **MEASURED cross-check:** `r = j - 1` on every one of
   384	the `1968` transitive `rho : G_{p,q} -> S_N` with `(p,q)` in
   385	`{(2,3),(2,5),(3,4),(3,5)}` and `N <= 5`; zero violations.
   386	
   387	### 5.2 `GAP[CUSP-CAGE-KUROSH-DIVISOR]`
   388	
   389	CUSP-CAGE writes `Delta ≅ F_r * (Z/p)^{*u} * (Z/q)^{*v}` with `u,v <= 1`.
   390	Two things are asserted there that Kurosh does not give.
   391	
   392	1. **The factors need not be full.** A Kurosh factor is a conjugate
   393	   intersection `Delta ∩ gZ/pg^{-1}`, hence `Z/d` for any `d | p`. In the
   394	   orbifold picture (`Z/p * Z/q = pi_1^{orb}` of a disc with cone points
   395	   `p, q`) a cone point of order `p` lifts to cone points of order `p/m_i`
   396	   with `sum m_i = M`; proper divisors genuinely occur.
   397	2. **`u <= 1` is not the right cyclicity condition.** What torsion-freeness
   398	   of `H^{ab}` forces (via CENTRAL-RANK: `Z^j / <zeta> ≅ Z^{j-1} (+) Z/n`)
   399	   is that the finite factors have **pairwise coprime** orders. Two
   400	   factors both dividing `p` are allowed when they are coprime — e.g.
   401	   `p = 6` with factors `Z/2` and `Z/3`.
   402	
   403	Consequence: CUSP-CAGE's congruences (`pq | M-1` in the `(u,v)=(1,1)`
   404	case, and the derived `N >= pq+1`) are stated at a scope narrower than
   405	their hypotheses support and must not be quoted at general `(p,q)`.
   406	What is **not** affected: `M >= 2` (if `M = 1` then `Delta ≅ Z/p * Z/q`
   407	has `r = 0`, so `j = 1` by CENTRAL-RANK, contradicting `j >= 2`), and
   408	CUSP-KILL itself, whose `M = 1` step uses rational Euler characteristic
   409	multiplicativity on `Delta ≅ Z/p * Z/q` directly. The corrected cage is
   410	§5.3–§5.4.
   411	
   412	### 5.3 THEOREM ORBIFOLD-CAGE
   413	
   414	Let `s` (resp. `s'`) be the number of preimages of the `p`- (resp. `q`-)
   415	cone point in the degree-`M` orbifold cover `Delta <= Z/p * Z/q`, with
   416	local degrees `m_1..m_s` (`m_i | p`, `sum m_i = M`) and `l_1..l_{s'}`
   417	(`l_j | q`, `sum l_j = M`).
   418	
   419	> **THEOREM ORBIFOLD-CAGE.** Assume `H^{ab}` torsion-free (Lemma F1).
   420	> Then
   421	> ```text
   422	> (C-1)  s + s' = M + 2 - j ;
   423	> (C-2)  the orders  {p/m_i > 1} ∪ {q/l_j > 1}  are pairwise coprime ;
   424	> (C-3)  gcd(p/m_i, kappa) = gcd(q/l_j, kappa) = 1  for all i, j ;
   425	> (C-4)  s = #cycles of rho(alpha) on N points,  s' = #cycles of rho(beta).
   426	> ```
   427	>
   428	> *Proof.* The cover orbifold has underlying compact surface of genus `g`
   429	> with `c >= 1` boundary circles, so `Delta ≅ F_{2g+c-1} * (finite cyclics)`
   430	> and `r = 2g+c-1`; CENTRAL-RANK gives `2g + c = j`. Multiplicativity of
   431	> `chi^{orb}`,
   432	> `(2-2g-c) - sum_i(1 - m_i/p) - sum_j(1 - l_j/q) = M(1/p + 1/q - 1)`,
   433	> reduces to `(C-1)` after substituting `sum_i m_i = sum_j l_j = M`.
   434	> `(C-2)`: `Delta^{ab}`'s torsion is `Z^j/<zeta> `'s torsion, hence cyclic.
   435	> For `(C-3)`–`(C-4)`: `rho(z)` is central in a transitive group, hence
   436	> semiregular of order `kappa` with `M` orbits (= blocks). On a block-orbit
   437	> of size `m_i`, `rho(alpha)^{m_i}` restricts to `rho(z)^{k_i}`, and
   438	> `rho(alpha)^p = rho(z)` forces `k_i (p/m_i) ≡ 1 (mod kappa)`; hence
   439	> `gcd(k_i,kappa) = 1`, which is `(C-3)`, and the block-orbit splits into
   440	> `gcd(k_i,kappa) = 1` point-orbits, which is `(C-4)`. ∎
   441	
   442	**MEASURED cross-check:** `(C-1)` holds on all `1968` reps of §5.1, and
   443	`(C-4)` on all `3321` reps over `(p,q) ∈ {(2,3),(2,5),(3,4),(3,5),(4,5)}`,
   444	`N <= 5` (zero violations, both).
   445	
   446	### 5.4 THEOREM CUSP-PARITY
   447	
   448	> **THEOREM CUSP-PARITY.** Let `eps := sgn rho(m)`. Then
   449	> ```text
   450	> eps = (-1)^{W - sum_l s_l} = (-1)^{sum_l s_l (mu_l - 1)} ,
   451	> sgn rho(alpha) = eps^q ,   sgn rho(beta) = eps^p ,
   452	> ```
   453	> equivalently `(-1)^{N-s} = eps^q` and `(-1)^{N-s'} = eps^p`.
   454	>
   455	> *Proof.* `sgn ∘ rho : G -> {±1}` factors through `G^{ab} = Z<m>`, and
   456	> `alpha |-> q m`, `beta |-> p m`. The first equality is the cycle type
   457	> `1^a prod_l mu_l^{s_l}` of (3.1). The reformulation uses
   458	> `sgn(sigma) = (-1)^{N - #cycles}` with `(C-4)`. ∎
   459	
   460	**MEASURED cross-check:** zero violations on `4947` reps across
   461	`(p,q) ∈ {(2,3),(2,5),(3,4),(3,5),(4,5),(3,7),(5,6)}`, `N <= 5`.
   462	
   463	This gate is cheap, all-degree, and it is what does most of the killing.
   464	
   465	### 5.5 THEOREM CUSP-A-EMPTY
   466	
   467	> **THEOREM CUSP-A-EMPTY.** Under `H2`, MPRIME case (A) is **empty** for
   468	> every `4 <= N <= 7`. At `N = 8` it is nonempty, with an explicit
   469	> survivor list.
   470	
   471	*Proof for `N = 4`.* N4-PIN gives `a = 2`, `W = 2`, one dicritical
   472	`(s_1,mu_1) = (1,2)`, so `rho(m)` has cycle type `(2,1,1)`, `eps = -1`.
   473	CUSP-KILL gives `j >= 2`, and `j <= a = 2`, so `j = 2`; CENTRAL-RANK gives
   474	`r = 1`; `M >= 2` and `M kappa = 4` give `M ∈ {2,4}`. `(C-1)`: `s + s' = M`.
   475	CUSP-PARITY with `N = 4` even: `s ≡ q` and `s' ≡ p (mod 2)`, so
   476	`M = s+s' ≡ p+q (mod 2)`; `M` is even, so **`p` and `q` are both odd**.
   477	Now the partitions:
   478	
   479	* `M = 2`: `s + s' = 2` forces `s = s' = 1`, i.e. `m_1 = 2 | p` — `p` even.
   480	  Contradiction.
   481	* `M = 4`: `s + s' = 4`. `(s,s') = (1,3)` needs `m_1 = 4 | p` — `p` even.
   482	  `(3,1)` needs `4 | q`. `(2,2)`: partitions of `4` into two parts are
   483	  `{2,2}` (needs `2|p`, even) and `{1,3}` (needs `3|p`, and cone orders
   484	  `p` and `p/3` are coprime only if `p = 3`); pairing `{1,3}` on the `p`
   485	  side with `{1,3}` on the `q` side needs `3 | gcd(p,q)`, and with `{2,2}`
   486	  on the `q` side needs `q` even. Every branch contradicts.
   487	
   488	Hence no admissible cell, and case (A) at `N = 4` is empty. ∎
   489	
   490	*Second, independent proof at `N = 4`.* Without the parity gate, the same
   491	partition analysis alone leaves exactly `(p,q) = (2,3)` (up to swap), with
   492	`M = 4`, `kappa = 1`, cone data `{2,2} | {1,3}`. But `G_{2,3}` is the
   493	trefoil group `B_3`, with `alpha = sigma_1 sigma_2 sigma_1`,
   494	`beta = sigma_1 sigma_2`, and `m = alpha beta^{-1} = sigma_2`
   495	(MEASURED identity on all `206` reps checked, together with
   496	`alpha^2 = beta^3` and `sigma_1 = alpha sigma_2 alpha^{-1}`). So `B_3` is
   497	generated by **two conjugates of the meridian**, and `rho(m)` is a
   498	transposition; two transpositions generate a group with orbits of size
   499	`<= 3`, never transitive on `4` letters (MEASURED for `N = 4,5,6`;
   500	elementary in general). Empty. ∎
   501	
   502	*Proof for `N = 5`.* `M | 5` and `M >= 2` give `M = 5`, `kappa = 1`;
   503	`a <= 3`, `j ∈ {2,3}`.
   504	`j = 2, a = 2`: `W = 3`, one dicritical `(1,3)`, `eps = +1`, so `s` and
   505	`s'` are both odd by CUSP-PARITY, while `(C-1)` gives `s + s' = 5`, odd —
   506	impossible.
   507	`j = 2, a = 3` (`W = 2`, `eps = -1`): `s+s' = 5`; the partitions of `5`
   508	into `(1,4),(2,3),(3,2),(4,1)` parts all fail `(C-2)` or coprimality
   509	(`(1,4)`: three equal cone orders `q`; `(2,3)` with `{1,4}`: forces
