   619	
   620	### 7.2 Negative control — an uncabled configuration where torsion fails
   621	
   622	Two, one proved and one measured.
   623	
   624	*Proved.* If `A` is nodal and transverse to `L_infty`, then
   625	`pi_1(P^2\A)` is abelian (Deligne–Fulton), so `pi_1(C^2\A) ≅ Z^{r}`;
   626	every finite-index subgroup of `Z^r` is `Z^r`. **No cover of such a
   627	complement ever has torsion, at any degree.** This is the exact
   628	theorem-level form of ID §5 step 1's "nodes contribute no torsion".
   629	
   630	*Measured, and nonabelian.* `d` concurrent lines in `C^2`: all `d` places
   631	at infinity are transverse (uncabled), and
   632	`pi_1(C^2\A) ≅ F_{d-1} × Z` is nonabelian.
   633	
   634	```text
   635	d = 3 :  k=2   7 transitive covers   Z^3 x4, Z^4 x3            no torsion
   636	         k=3  44                     Z^3 x18, Z^5 x26          no torsion
   637	         k=4 666                     Z^3 x96, Z^4 x144, Z^6 x426  no torsion
   638	d = 4 :  k=2  15 / k=3 248 / k=4 14586                          no torsion
   639	```
   640	
   641	`15,566` transitive covers of uncabled complements, zero torsion —
   642	against `30/54` with torsion on the cabled trefoil complement at `k = 4`.
   643	The contrast is real; the inference from it is not (§2.2).
   644	
   645	### 7.3 Enumeration soundness
   646	
   647	The cage enumerator is exhaustive in `(p,q)` for a reason, not a bound:
   648	`D_i := p/m_i`. If two `D_i > 1` they are coprime and both divide `p`, so
   649	`D_i D_{i'} | p` and each `D | m ≤ M`, giving `p ≤ M^2`. If exactly one
   650	`D_{i_0} > 1` and `s >= 2`, every other `m_i = p`, so `p ≤ M`. If all
   651	`D_i = 1`, `p = M/s`. Only `s = 1` is unbounded, and then `p = M·D` with
   652	`D` free, entering the rest of the cage only through `gcd(MD,q) = 1`,
   653	`gcd(D,kappa) = 1` and the parity of `p`. In that family the meridian
   654	exponent `f` is constant modulo the order of `rho(beta)` (e.g. at `N = 7`,
   655	`p = 2`, `q = 7D`: `2f ≡ 1 (mod 7)` gives `f ≡ 4` for every `D`), so the
   656	whole family collapses to one test. That collapse is *observed* to hold —
   657	the `N = 8` family `q = 4,20,...,196` gives identical survivor data at
   658	every member — but it is not proved, which is why `N >= 7` is typed
   659	MEASURED and `N <= 6` PROVED.
