./xmodel/block-descent-a1-rank4-reducible-component-tree-ledger-hostile-review-sol56-20260831.log:301:*Proof.* Chau 2004 Lemma 1 realises every irreducible component of `A_F` as `f_phi(C)` for a dicritical series `phi`. Each such component is therefore the image of at least one dicritical line `l subset L_F`, and `mu_l >=1` because `deg f_phi>0`. Orevkov's identity then gives `N-1 = 3 >= sum_l mu_l >= #Irr(A_F)`. Every component of `B` equals a component of `A_F`, so `m<=3`. Extra `A_F` components not in `B` only tighten the inequality. QED.
