./xmodel/mprime-alln-review-gpt55-20260902.log:9945:xmodel/ideation-20260831T1033Z-grok46.md:110:**Setup, from promoted facts only.** An actual rank-four proper block has irreducible reduced charged branch `B`, `normalization(B)=A1`, and generic branch partition `(2,1,1)` or `(3,1)` with one ramification point (`H_inertia` at `5d7df7ce…:84–104`, consumed by the `m=1` integration). So a generic point of `B subset A_F` has fibre cycle type either one 2-cycle plus two 1-cycles, or one 3-cycle plus one 1-cycle. Write `B^sm` for the smooth locus of `B`. The unique ramified preimage along generic `B` is the ramified sheet. The complementary preimages form an unramified covering `Sigma -> B^sm` of degree 2 in the `(2,1,1)` case and degree 1 in the `(3,1)` case. These are *sheets of the finite map*, not dicritical divisors and not flags of a compactification. Flag/place/series: this covering is not identified with an Orevkov dicritical, nor with a physical place of `B`, nor with the cover series of a splice diagram.
./xmodel/mprime-alln-review-gpt55-20260902.log:9948:xmodel/ideation-20260831T1033Z-grok46.md:229:**Dependencies.** Promoted `m=1`; promoted `H_inertia` (generic partition `(2,1,1)` or `(3,1)`, one ramification point, `normalization(B)=A1`); conjugacy sentence C1 of the one-node packet (mandatory in citations, harvest §4); Chau 2003 Lemma 5 (`A_F` = images of dicritical series); Assi–García-Sánchez δ-sequence dictionary. Does *not* depend on (2.3), Prop. 4.3, C3, inverse-Kummer, or any reducible-row lemma.
