./xmodel/domrina-1999-audit-sol56-20260901.log:14558:     4	**Question.** Can a Keller map `F:C^2 -> C^2` (Jacobian a nonzero constant, not invertible) have a *trivial dicritical*: a dicritical divisor `l` at infinity whose image closure is an affine curve (a component of the non-properness set `A_F`) and whose generic local degree is `mu_l = 1` — equivalently, by Lemma 4.2 of the charged day’s SHEET-GATE writeup, a divisorial valuation `v` at infinity with `v(dx∧dy)=0` that is dicritical for `F` with affine image?
./xmodel/domrina-1999-audit-sol56-20260901.log:14609:    55	## 3. Fetched primary literature (Abhyankar series, Cassou-Noguès, Lê–Weber, Gwoździewicz, Jelonek, …)
./xmodel/domrina-1999-audit-sol56-20260901.log:14619:    65	| Jelonek, *The set of points at which a polynomial map is not proper*, Ann. Polon. Math. **58** (1993), 259–266 | `http://matwbn.icm.edu.pl/ksiazki/apm/apm58/apm5834.pdf` | `30b497466c1c27923a918db1c7277e90485667647fb3f2d6505f3f2c26ef420e` |
