./xmodel/block-descent-a1-one-cusp-wild-valuation-structure-sol56-20260831.log:853:xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:354:**First falsification test.** In local model (5.1), `Disc(P)=unit (u^mu-v^mu)^2` is affine and of length proportional to `mu` along the coincidence divisor. That model has no “infinity.” If a global compactification can hide the same length on affine `C0` (which it can: `C0` is affine), the degree bound does not force infinity. The test is whether the **global** identity (4.7) of `bcc5148...` plus properness of `H` forbids supporting all of `I_t` on `C0 cap V`. A single consistent degree count that places `I_t` on `C0` falsifies the infinity-forcing half.
