./xmodel/block-descent-a1-quartic-cycle1-pseudoplane-companion-hostile-review-opus5-20260830.log:17:**Primary-source work** (narrow checks; Miyanishi fetched to `/tmp`, hash matching the charged cubic funnel's recorded value): Lemma 1.4.16 and 1.4.3 verified verbatim and confirmed degree-free; the `Pic(U)=Z/μ⟨Φ⟩` generator claim needs Lemma 1.4.3(3), not Corollary 1.4.4; Theorem 2.5.10's typed conclusion is `r ≡ 2 (mod d)`, not `r = 2` — a source erratum the charged cubic funnel inherits. In Żołądek: the `td≤5` appeal is over-charged (Domrina–Orevkov degree ≤4 suffices, cited on p. 432), and Lemma 6.2 (p. 457) independently *predicts* the omitted node as a self-intersection of the non-properness curve, killing that line of attack.
./xmodel/reducible-all-n-verification-grok46-20260901.md:139:Charged statement: `deg A_F` admits no bound in terms of `N`, via `T(x,y)=(x, y+x^k)` acting on the target. Re-derived.
./xmodel/reducible-all-n-verification-grok46-20260901.md:153:So `T_k ∘ F` is Keller. Geometric degree: for generic `(a,b)`, the fibre of `T_k ∘ F` over `(a,b)` is the fibre of `F` over `(a, b−a^k)`; `T_k` is bijective, so the two generic fibre-cardinalities agree. Non-proper value set: `q` is a non-proper value of `T_k ∘ F` iff some `p_n→∞` has `T_k(F(p_n))→q` iff `F(p_n)→T_k^{-1}(q)` (homeomorphism of `C^2`) iff `T_k^{-1}(q) ∈ A_F`. Thus `A_{T_k ∘ F} = T_k(A_F)`.
./xmodel/reducible-all-n-verification-grok46-20260901.md:161:This is a family of target automorphisms, not a family of Keller maps constructed from scratch. Operationally: there is no function `B(N)` such that every noninvertible Keller map of geometric degree `N` has `deg A_F ≤ B(N)`, because any one such `F` with `A_F ≠ ∅` (and noninvertible Keller maps are not proper, so `A_F ≠ ∅`) produces `T_k ∘ F` of the same `N` and unbounded degree. Floor/attainment: this is the absence of a ceiling, not an exact degree formula. It does not realise any SS9 class; it only says raw `deg A_F` is not a gate. The `d_min` restatement in charged SS6 is the surviving form.
./xmodel/reducible-all-n-verification-grok46-20260901.md:171:Packet `(1,0)^5`. Budget: five trivials, `Σ W = 5 = N−1`, `K=0`. Every meridian has cycle type `1^6` (all `μ=1`, `s=1`), so `ρ` is trivial. The covering `C^2 \ F^{-1}(A_F) → C^2 \ A_F` would be 6 disjoint copies. Both total space and base are complements of curves in `C^2`, hence connected. Contradiction. The packet is dead. (IND) is consistent rather than obstructive: `Σ ι = 5−0−5 = 0`. The kill is transitivity, not the budget.
./xmodel/reducible-all-n-verification-grok46-20260901.md:219:| 3 | NO-DEG-CAP family | **HOLDS** | `T_k(x,y)=(x,y+x^k)`: Jac=1, inverse polynomial; `Jac(T_k∘F)=Jac(F)`; geometric degree preserved by fibre translation `(a,b)↦(a,b−a^k)`; `A_{T_k∘F}=T_k(A_F)`; `(μ,corr,s)` preserved; `deg T_k(D)` unbounded once `deg_y f ≥1`. Absence of a ceiling, not an attainment. |
