./xmodel/horn-flagship-opus5-20260902.log:6:**(1) The (B3) group.** The charge's presentation claim — "torus-knot group with `k` added commuting-square relators" — is false, and I replaced it rather than deriving it. `G = pi_1(C^2\A_F)` has `n = deg_y bar A_F` ZvK generators, unbounded in `(p,q,k)`; only the inclusion `iota: Loc_{p_0} = G_{p,q} -> G` is canonical, and HT's NO-PUSHFORWARD forbids transporting across it. The commuting-square reading of the double points is correct exactly when they are genuine nodes (contact `t=1`); contact `t` gives `(x_i x_j)^t = (x_j x_i)^t`.
./xmodel/horn-flagship-opus5-20260902.log:8:Of the three theorems: **CUSP-PARITY survives strictly stronger** (`sgn rho(h) = eps^{deg h}` for every `h`, since `G^ab = Z`); **ORBIFOLD-CAGE survives orbit-summed** (`c_A + c_B = M_tot + T - R_tot`, with `r_O = 0` at affine orbits because `F` étale forces `(E,y) ≅ (A_F,p_0)`); **CENTRAL-RANK is refuted globally** — `G` has no centre in (B3) — and survives only per-orbit. Two new laws (B3-PUSHOFF, B3-COMPONENT) were needed and proved.
./xmodel/horn-flagship-opus5-20260902.log:10:**(2) The cage on (B3): rigid, not empty.** At `N=4` it pins `rho(G) = S_4`, forces the cusp Puiseux pair to satisfy `(2|p, 3|q)` or `(3|p, 2|q)`, and determines `E` completely (`j=1`, genus `k_odd−1`, one cusp, `3+4k−2k_odd` ends; or `j=2` with both components rational when all contacts are even). `j=1` is *not* a kill here — Lin–Zaidenberg fails since `E ≇ A_F` — so I found no EMPTY window in `N` and did not manufacture one.
