./xmodel/websweep-0823.log:6477: | EC-K3-Q80-UNMARKED-FIRST-Q4-COLLISION | Exact unmarked first q4 collision on the rational Q80 coefficient curve | The exact rational coefficient curve reconstructed from the slope-8/87 Q80 branch lies identically on the degree-eight first-q4 collision divisor: direct substitution in QQ(u) is zero. The explicit first-neighbor coordinate U=(x-T)/T^2 therefore has finite I5 at U=d(u)-1. At the exact rational witness u=0, the fifth but not sixth discriminant factor is present, the remaining degree-eight finite factor is squarefree, and A and B are units; these nonvanishings prove the generic configuration over QQ(u). Degree checks give I5* at infinity, so the unmarked first child has I5*+I5+8I1 and root lattice D9+A4. This does not construct global marked sections, a second or later pencil, a rootless MW17 equation, a bisection, an extension collision, or a generic rank-19 family. | [source](elkies-k3/BISECTION_COLLISION_SEARCH.md) | — | [checker](elkies-k3/scripts/verify_q80_unmarked_first_q4_collision_qq.sage) | exact_symbolic; `sha256:283249cc83b4…`; locks: `elkies-k3/scripts/derive_q80_first_q4_pencil.sage`, `elkies-k3/scripts/verify_q80_unmarked_first_q4_collision_qq.sage`; updates: consumers `REPRODUCE.md`, `elkies-k3/BISECTION_COLLISION_SEARCH.md` | — |
./xmodel/websweep-0823.log:6478: | EC-ICARM-CONSTRUCTION-FINGERPRINTS | Bounded exact construction recognition for ICARM curves 273 and 281--286 | For ICARM curves 273, 281, 282, 285 and 286, exact Weierstrass invariants, point-denominator fingerprints and repository-wide exact-j comparisons are pinned. The exact degree-twelve equation in z=T^2 is solved for every member of the complete 2329-family normalized nonsingular six-root Mestre census of diameter at most 300 and for the larger normalized Fermigier control tuple. The only exact match is curve 282 at roots (0,29,658,722,981,1036) and T=11671/21; curves 273, 281, 285 and 286 have no match in this bounded census. All five curves have independently certified trivial rational torsion, excluding direct specialization of the implemented Elkies--Klagsbrun model with its forced point (0,0) of order two. These conclusions do not exclude larger or generalized Mestre tuples, Kihara/Nagao families, K3 descendants, isogenous images or private families; denominator patterns are diagnostics rather than construction certificates. | [source](elliptic-curves/notes/ICARM_7FFF_ZIP_SEQUENCE.md) | `ECR30` | [checker](elliptic-curves/cas/analyze_icarm_construction_fingerprints.py) | exact_symbolic; `sha256:154895accc1f…`; locks: `requirements.txt`; updates: narrows problems `OP-EC-NEXT` | — |
./xmodel/websweep-0823.log:6479: | EC-K3-H3-Q8-QQ-D13 | Exact corrected H3 q8 neighbour over QQ with D13/MW4 child | On the exact H3 q6 E8+E6/MW3 child, the binary-quartic covariant is treated as a degree-two covering map, giving the primitive q8 marked section S=Pmap+Qmap with Mordell--Weil coordinate (-2,-2,0), height 24, zero intersection 10 and smooth collision divisor of degree ten. Clearing the full rational q-frame, including the Dx factor of x(S)=Nx/Dx, gives a 13-dimensional characteristic-zero Riemann--Roch ambient with eleven independent conditions and a two-dimensional pencil. Exact elimination produces a degree-four quartic whose Jacobian has one I9* fibre, nine I1 fibres and smooth infinity; hence its root lattice is D13 and its Mordell--Weil rank is four in Picard rank nineteen. This proves the second equation-level H3 neighbour E8+E6/MW3 -> D13/MW4. It does not construct the eleven later equation-level neighbours to the rootless MW17 frame or identify curve 273 as a specialization. | [source](elkies-k3/H3_Q8_REAUDIT_2026-08-22.md) | `EC-K3-H3-Q6`, `EC-K3-H3-Q8-CHILD-MARKING` | [checker](elkies-k3/scripts/derive_h92_q6_child_q8_corrected2cover_qq.sage) | exact_symbolic; `sha256:01da6b84ee1f…`; locks: `elkies-k3/data/fibrations/h3_q8_component_nef_physical_root_target.json`, `elkies-k3/scripts/derive_h92_q6_child_q8_corrected2cover_qq.sage`; updates: narrows problems `OP-EC-NEXT` | — |
./xmodel/websweep-0823.log:6480:-| EC-K3-H3-D13-MW17-LATTICE-CHAIN | Exact eleven-step nef degree-two H3 lattice chain from D13/MW4 to rootless/MW17 | Starting from the exact D13/MW4 frame of EC-K3-H3-Q8-QQ-D13, eleven stored primitive integral U-neighbours with q-sequence (24,6,8,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,6) give D12/MW5, A11/MW6, 2A5/MW7, 3A3/MW8, A3+2A2/MW10, 5A1/MW12, 4A1/MW13, 3A1/MW14, 2A1/MW15, A1/MW16, and finally a rootless MW17 frame. Every factor presentation has old-fibre degree two. Independent reconstruction from the pinned witnesses checks every child Gram matrix and a determinant-one composite transport. Exact chamber checkers prove all eleven selected classes nef using finite-component degrees, full-frame closest-vector calculations, and the degree-two bisection parity identity. The final q6 witness comes from a bounded search, but the displayed witness, child, and nefness are exact; no exhaustive q4 or global minimal-q claim is made. This certifies the complete lattice/chamber chain only. The eleven equation-level characteristic-zero pencils after D13/MW4, transported sections, and specialization to curve 273 remain open. | [source](elliptic-curves/notes/ICARM_CURVE273_CONSTRUCTION_INVESTIGATION.md) | `EC-K3-H3-Q8-QQ-D13` | [checker](elkies-k3/scripts/verify_h3_d13_to_mw17_path.sage) | exact_symbolic; `sha256:3a3a1b51553c…`; locks: `elkies-k3/scripts/exact_neighbor_engine.sage`, `elkies-k3/scripts/analyze_h3_d13_q4_chamber.sage`, `elkies-k3/scripts/analyze_h3_rank_growing_degree2_chain.sage`, `elkies-k3/scripts/analyze_h3_mw10_to_rootless_chambers.sage`, `elkies-k3/scripts/verify_h3_d13_to_mw17_path.sage`, `artifacts/generated-results/elkies-k3-h3-d13-to-mw17-path.json`; updates: narrows problems `OP-EC-NEXT`; consumers `REPRODUCE.md`, `elkies-k3/KUMAR_E7E8_BACKTRACK.md`, `elliptic-curves/notes/ICARM_CURVE273_CONSTRUCTION_INVESTIGATION.md` | — |
./xmodel/websweep-0823.log:6481:+| EC-K3-H3-Q24-EXACT-SECTION | Exact H3 D13 q24 horizontal section over QQ | For the selected H3 D13/MW4 orbit85 q24 continuation, the modular degree-46 section at p=100003 is lifted by a structured 24-by-24 p-adic Newton system from precision 2048 to precision 8192. Rational reconstruction resolves all 156 live section coefficients with 136067 modulus bits, and the resulting characteristic-zero section satisfies the exact Weierstrass identity and the modular regression. The exported section has deg(Z,X,Y)=(24,52,78) and affine denominator degrees (48,72). This proves the exact horizontal q24 section only; it does not yet construct the D12/MW5 child equation, resolved-RR pencil, binary-quartic Jacobian, fibre certificate, or later corridor hops. | [source](REPRODUCE.md) | `EC-K3-H3-Q8-QQ-D13`, `EC-K3-H3-D13-MW17-LATTICE-CHAIN` | [checker](elkies-k3/scripts/lift_q24_structured_newton.sage) | exact_symbolic; `sha256:3d3d425b933a…`; locks: `elkies-k3/scripts/lift_q24_structured_newton.sage`, `artifacts/local/elkies-k3/q8-q24-horizontal-section-qq.json` | — |
./xmodel/websweep-0823.log:6482:+| EC-K3-H3-D13-MW17-LATTICE-CHAIN | Exact lossless reverse Neron--Severi transport from pinned R17 to H3 | The H3 q6/q8 entrance followed by eleven stored primitive integral U-neighbours with q-sequence (24,6,8,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,6) gives the selected nef degree-two lattice corridor from H3 E7+E8/MW2 through D13/MW4 to a rootless MW17 frame. Every suffix factor presentation has old-fibre degree two, and exact chamber checkers prove nefness. A pinned determinant-one positive-frame isometry C now identifies the formerly unnamed rootless endpoint F with the recovered rank17 Gram P by C^t*P*C=F. Inverting the complete determinant-one 19-dimensional composite gives an explicit integral R with R*(U+(-P))*R^t=U+(-H3), and a generated fourteen-stage ledger retains every full frame, incoming transition and inverse, and every stage basis in both H3 and pinned-R17 coordinates. The ledger separately retains an exact full-NS bridge between the first dominant D13 representative used by the lattice corridor and the unequal component-nef D13 representative used by the q8 equation route; that bridge changes the embedded U, so these marked elliptic fibrations are not interchangeable by their common D13/MW4 label. The final q6 witness comes from a bounded search, but the displayed witness, child, nefness, endpoint isometry, and reverse transport are exact; no exhaustive q4, global minimal-q, or optimal-route claim is made. This is a lattice/marking certificate only. The eleven equation-level characteristic-zero pencils after D13/MW4, explicit transported section functions, and specialization to curve 273 remain open. | [source](elkies-k3/RANK17_TO_H3_REVERSE_TRANSPORT_2026-08-23.md) | `EC-K3-H3-Q8-QQ-D13` | [checker](elkies-k3/scripts/verify_rank17_to_h3_reverse_transport.sage) | exact_symbolic; `sha256:78c22521c010…`; locks: `elkies-k3/scripts/exact_neighbor_engine.sage`, `elkies-k3/scripts/analyze_h3_first_q6_chamber.sage`, `elkies-k3/scripts/classify_h3_